From 94c743bf8cda464b2bab094064c3c694c13528b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 18:10:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Measure item 3-2, and collect the signal 4-1 left out
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3-2's premise is one sentence — "shapeSlots holds JSValue references, so
`vector.x = 1.5` allocates" — and it names a cause. Taken literally as a probe,
the line allocates and the slot does not: `o.x = 2` costs 0.00 bytes an
iteration, because storing an already-boxed value into a slot is a reference
copy. What the example pays for is the LITERAL, which VisitLiteral re-boxes on
every evaluation and which item 3-1 measured at 1.2% of the corpus's boxing.
The slot's own 32 B appears only in the row the item does not write —
`o.x = v * 1.5`, where the value is a raw double at the point of the store.

The field rows equal the element rows to the hundredth: 31.98 for a read into
an addition, 96.00 for a read-modify-write, in an array and in an object field
alike. 3-1 and 3-2 are not twins by analogy; they are one mechanism — a value
that stays unboxed from producer to consumer — with two storage backends.

Their populations are disjoint, and counting that needed item 4-1's third
signal, "numeric-vs-generic per site", which 4-1 deliberately left uncollected
and 3-8 named as the missing instrument. It is one IsNumber test on the inline
cache's two hit returns. Over the corpus, 50.1% of cache-answered reads hand
back a number — and the per-suite column is what decides the plan: 98% of
those are Box2D's (9 853 002 of 18 241 436 reads, 54.0%), while NavierStokes
performs 388 property reads, zero of them numeric, and mints 29 977 471 boxes.
Crypto reads 651 289 and mints 42 423 644.

So 3-1 carries 85% of the corpus's boxes and 3-2 carries Box2D's 11.6 M, no
work on shape slots reaches NavierStokes or Crypto at all, and the shared
compiler half should be built once. `vector.x = 1.5` should be struck from the
item's rationale: it pointed at the wrong half of its own mechanism for as
long as it stood unmeasured.

Adds cacheHitsNumeric to PropertyOptimizationDiagnostics (off by default with
the rest) and six `field` rows to --local-alloc. No behaviour change.
